third_party/headless_browser is a copy of https://github.com/xpzouying/headless_browser v0.4.0
(MIT License, third_party/headless_browser/LICENSE) with one change: the --no-sandbox flag is optional.

Changes in this distribution (branch ma/patches) include: separate read and write bearer tokens,
loopback-only listening, MCP endpoint off by default, no CORS, reduced HTTP routes, private
atomic cookie writes, one browser operation at a time, browser sandbox kept on macOS,
structured timeout and page-access error codes, comment submission receipts with idempotency
keys, reply attribution on notifications, reading one comment thread with its replies, deleting the account's own comment (ported from liaogx), read-only private message listing, reading and replying in existing private conversations (no new conversations), publishing notes with a content-type declaration (e.g. AI-generated content), visibility and declaration read back before publishing, publish receipts with the note id, a publish-page inspection that never publishes, and search
waiting for result hydration instead of full-page stability (ported from upstream PRs #835 and #839).
Original authors are not responsible for these modifications.
